WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Hi, I'm Abhishek, and this is Funnel of Thought

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.040
— built for the Agents of SigNoz hackathon.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.760
The idea: AI agents have a reasoning contract

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.020
— mine is plan, tool, validate, respond — and

5
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.440
nothing today measures whether they honour it.

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.253
So I built three things: an OpenTelemetry-instrumented

7
00:00:17.273 --> 00:00:21.933
LangGraph agent; fot, a CLI that turns SigNoz

8
00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:24.180
Trace Funnels into funnels-as-code over reasoning

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.540
steps; and signoz-funnel-mcp — the funnel tools

10
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.680
SigNoz's MCP server doesn't ship.

11
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.880
All of it runs on self-hosted SigNoz, installed with Foundry.

12
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.440
My agent has a validation step. A dashboard told me it ran

13
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.700
in one hundred percent of runs. A funnel over the same

14
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.840
one hundred and twenty-five traces said sixty-four percent.

15
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.780
Same traces. Both queries correct.

16
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.680
Only one asked the right question.

17
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.020
Here's the funnel, live, over the agent's

18
00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.400
reasoning. One twenty-five runs start.

19
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.100
One twenty-five reach the tool call.

20
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.620
Then the cliff: only eighty reach

21
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.240
validate, in order. Sixty-four percent.

22
00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.680
And the counts are printed on every bar — a

23
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.760
percentage without a denominator isn't evidence.

24
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.180
This isn't my tool marking its own homework — here's

25
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.200
the same funnel inside SigNoz itself.

26
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.140
Sixty-four percent. One twenty-five, one twenty-five,

27
00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:27.140
eighty, eighty. Down thirty-six percent on step three.

28
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.980
Trace Funnels are a SigNoz primitive. No

29
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.460
other observability backend ships one.

30
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.744
So why did the counter say one hundred?

31
00:01:35.764 --> 00:01:39.560
A counter only asks: did the span exist. A funnel

32
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.320
asks: did it happen after the previous step.

33
00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.120
Forty-five runs emitted their validate span

34
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.360
before the tool result existed — the agent

35
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.680
validated an answer that hadn't arrived yet.

36
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.680
A counter measures presence. A funnel measures

37
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.500
sequence. Ordering lives in the trace, not the span.

38
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.020
Here's one of those runs. Plan — then validate,

39
00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.420
in red — and only then the tool call.

40
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:07.380
It finished validating before the

41
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.580
thing it was validating existed.

42
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.680
None of SigNoz's forty-one MCP tools reach

43
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.920
funnels, so I shipped the missing ones.

44
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.080
Here, the agent calls get-funnel-analytics

45
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.100
and reads its own conversion rate.

46
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.240
The read path has no model in it — it's

47
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.460
sub-second, deterministic, and free.

48
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.500
What did I learn? Funnels need strictly increasing

49
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.480
timestamps. Two correct specs can be silently incompatible

50
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.940
— that finding is now two SigNoz issues and a pull request.

51
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.820
And agents fail politely: no errors, just skipped homework.

52
00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.700
So: watch validate-step conversion, and alert

53
00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.360
on the cliff. Mine is firing right now.
